; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; Memory two bindings can share, and blocking on a word in it
; (`stdlib/Chan.ax`, docs/memory-model.md MM-PAR-10). `Sys.ax` branches
; on `waitWordKind`, never on an OS name. The mmap/munmap numbers are
; the emitted runtime's own (`targetMmapNum`, `targetMunmapNum`), and
; `scripts/check-platform-constants.sh` compares them. The flags, the
; wait kind and the wait/wake numbers are checked only by running:
; `scripts/check-chan.sh` on Linux and Darwin.
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
;; no mapping: there is no kernel
(pub :: sysMmapNum Int)
(pub fn (sysMmapNum)
  Internal.Platform::impl_sysMmapNum)

;; no mapping: there is no kernel
